<doclang xmlns="https://www.doclang.ai/ns/v0" version="0.8"><!-- formula --><text><location value="64"/><location value="210"/><location value="436"/><location value="248"/><content>In summary, the model is described by equations (3.1)-(3.4). The aim is to solve them for the unknowns </content><formula>(p, q, r, s)</formula><content>. Using (3.6) and (3.5), we then obtain </content><formula>(u, v, w, s, \alpha)</formula>. The following section presents two example families of solutions to these equations.</text><!-- inline_key_value --><field_region><field_item><text><key>Invoice no.:</key><content> </content><value>2026-0042</value></text></field_item><field_item><text><key><bold>Issued</bold>:</key><content> </content><value>15 March 2026</value><content> (</content><value><italic>payable on receipt</italic></value>)</text></field_item></field_region><!-- inline_runs --><text><content>Water is </content>H<subscript>2</subscript>O, and CO<subscript>2</subscript><content> is a gas.</content></text><text>Held on the 21<superscript>st</superscript><content> of June, see </content><italic>the agenda</italic>.</text><text><content>Some </content><bold><content>bold </content></bold><content>text with </content><code>code</code><content> inside.</content></text><!-- list_and_table --><list><ldiv/><content>First </content><bold>item</bold><ldiv/><italic>Second</italic><content> item</content></list><table><fcel/><content>a </content><bold>b</bold><fcel/>c<nl/></table><!-- kept_content --><text><content> Indented</content><content> by one space, a run of  two, and </content><bold>a line</bold><content>
break.</content></text><!-- paragraph --><text><location value="12"/><location value="40"/><location value="300"/><location value="58"/><content>See </content><italic>Table 2</italic><content> for the values of </content><formula>\beta</formula>.</text></doclang>
